  "limitations": [
    "Acceptance is limited to the original G0-T10 fixed cloud release/recovery primitive. It does not certify production Turn/WorkspaceAgent, invite login, billing, or M1-M5 completion.",
    "The original v3 startup-failure remains failed/unconfirmed and its run remains closed; the independent fixed native entrypoint probe supplies new exit-42 evidence without replaying or rewriting that attempt.",
    "The rollout hold was observed running before replacement; afterwards the process was missing and lifecycle lastStop was null. Exact termination time, OS signal and successful completion are not established. Acceptance relies on replacement/version evidence and committed-checkpoint recovery, not an invented precise interruption.",
    "Completion uses a new supervisor to call the existing W1 ReleaseSandbox namespace. It does not claim the original closed W1 ReleaseHost coordinator resumed.",
    "The native fault tests a real entrypoint failure before readiness on the approved image, not a corrupt image pull or every possible startup failure.",
    "The API-after application health aggregates are not used as proof of final inactivity; the later per-instance API at 10:15:46 UTC shows all seven records inactive.",
    "No new model calls were issued by this review. Fixed probe source and bindings have no model access; modelDispatches:0 is not independent account billing evidence, and actual cash charges remain unverified.",
    "Review read saved remote receipts only and did not issue fresh cloud, VM or provider requests. Hash stability does not expand any original gate scope; earlier DNS, public slow-upload and production-identity limitations remain unchanged."
